-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bc6"}, {"id": "3ced29", "text": "A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bc7"}, {"id": "86dbf9", "text": "A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bc8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bc9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["6162fbaf6ed13040ec851d20"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>: A mixture of chloroform and aniline can be separated by simple distillation.</p><p>Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>: When separating aniline from a mixture of aniline and water by steam distillation aniline boils below its boiling point.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "245296", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bca"}, {"id": "24e8b4", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;is true but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bcb"}, {"id": "7caa44", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;is false but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bcc"}, {"id": "832123", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bcd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bce", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3a9"], "concepts": ["6162fbac6ed13040ec851b25"], "question": {"text": "The correct stability order of the following species/molecules is:\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FgneugorFe1HeiXVrfvu-0iUn7UZJWhboqObjJsW653Y.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "e4cc87", "text": "$q\\gt r\\gt p$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bcf"}, {"id": "99a024", "text": "$r\\gt q\\gt p$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bd0"}, {"id": "5a4c02", "text": "$q\\gt p\\gt r$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bd1"}, {"id": "e2019b", "text": "$\\mathrm{p}\\gt\\mathrm{q}\\gt\\mathrm{r}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bd2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bd3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4787"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ef8"], "question": {"text": "The isomeric deuterated bromide with molecular formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mi>DBr</mi></math> having two chiral carbon atoms is"}, "options": [{"id": "137c33", "text": "2-Bromo-1-deuterobutane", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bd4"}, {"id": "fd60f0", "text": "2-Bromo-2-deuterobutane", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f392ee0e063d9253bd5"}, {"id": "75f3a6", "text": "2-Bromo-3-deuterobutane", "i